  "description": "Repro attempt for a user-reported live-game artifact: 'black radiating middle or edges of a wall block' on the walls of an enclosed, regularly-roofed room -- described as a regression from something fixed before. Six TorchLamps are clustered tight against one corner of a sealed 21x21 roofed room (RoofConstructed, not thick) so their coverage overlaps as heavily as possible right where two wall runs meet, stressing both the indoor-occlusion vertex passes and the vector-light mask's saturation-correction fold at the same cells. A lone seventh lamp sits in the opposite corner as an unstressed control. Every SetFeature is left at its shipped default -- no manual overrides -- because the bug report is about the mod as subscribers actually run it.",
